    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized intelligence assessment reveals a U.S. military posture characterized by sustained global mobility, regional engagement, and adaptive deployment strategies. Carrier strike groups remain central to power projection, with USS Theodore Roosevelt (CVN-71) operating in the Pacific following RIMPAC 2026 and USS George Washington (CVN-73) conducting a historic port visit to Da Nang, Vietnam, accompanied by USS Robert Smalls (CG-62) and USS Shoup (DDG-86). This underscores the U.S. commitment to Indo-Pacific partnerships and regional stability. Strategic airlift operations, including C-17 and C-5M flights across the Atlantic and Pacific, indicate ongoing global mobility and rapid deployment capabilities, while high-altitude ISR platforms such as the Global 5000 and C-30J Spartan suggest enhanced electronic warfare and intelligence-gathering activities. Maritime patrol aircraft, particularly P-8 Poseidons operating over the Gulf Coast and central U.S., reflect sustained counter-narcotics and regional security missions, potentially aligned with NORAD objectives. The inactivation of USS Georgia (SSGN-729) signals a transition in submarine deployment strategies, prioritizing newer platforms. Overall, the data depicts a dynamic military environment with a focus on the Pacific and Atlantic theaters, reduced Middle East presence, and continued emphasis on interoperability with allied forces. Unusual patterns, such as the dispersion of training and calibration flights across the continental U.S., suggest routine but critical operational readiness activities.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
